By Hetty McKinnon (NYT Cooking)

While making fried rice the traditional way isn’t hard, this sheet-pan version is an excellent alternative method: It uses the oven for the heavy lifting and produces the perfect amount of crisping. Fried rice is the ultimate adaptable dish, and here, frozen mixed vegetables — that bag of corn, carrots, peas and beans that home cooks should always keep in the freezer — create a colorful canvas for an XO-inspired vegan mu…";}s:8:"relation";a:1:{s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}}s:10:"persistent";a:4:{s:4:"date";a:1:{s:7:"created";i:1679148552;}s:7:"creator";s:21:"Melissa Clepper-Faith";s:4:"user";s:3:"mcf";s:11:"last_change";a:8:{s:4:"date";i:1679148552;s:2:"ip";s:13:"75.165.224.98";s:4:"type";s:1:"C";s:2:"id";s:28:"recipes:sheet_pan_fried_rice";s:4:"user";s:3:"mcf";s:3:"sum";s:7:"created";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";s:10:"sizechange";i:2949;}}}